@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il29-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il29-time`
IMPORT `ito-s1-israeli-resident-individual`
IMPORT `ito-s1-israeli-resident-body`
IMPORT `ito-s1-foreign-resident`
IMPORT `ito-il29-test-people`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Row IL-29 tests: s 1 "Israeli resident" (b) (a body of persons) and "foreign resident" (with its second limb).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the Hebrew text BEFORE the code was run; the arithmetic is in the
-- comment beside it.  A failing assertion is a finding: none has been edited to match the code.
-- ===========================================================================

`D` MEANS `the default readings of row IL-29`

§ `A body of persons, (b)`

GIVEN y     IS A NUMBER
      inc   IS A BOOLEAN
      ctl   IS A `How long a connection with Israel lasted in the tax year`
GIVETH A `A body of persons in a tax year`
`a body in` y `, incorporated in Israel:` inc `, control and management in Israel:` ctl MEANS
    `A body of persons in a tax year` WITH
        `the tax year` IS `the calendar tax year` y
        `it was incorporated in Israel` IS inc
        `the control and management of its business were exercised in Israel` IS ctl
        `the control and management in Israel were exercised by an individual who became a first-time resident or a veteran returning resident, or by someone on his behalf` IS FALSE
        `the day that individual became an Israeli resident` IS NOTHING
        `that individual elected the adjustment year of section 14(b)` IS FALSE
        `the day that individual arrived in Israel` IS NOTHING
        `it would not have been an Israeli resident had the control and management not been exercised in Israel by such an individual or on his behalf` IS FALSE
        `the body of persons asked otherwise` IS FALSE

`bres` MEANS FALSE

GIVEN b IS A `A body of persons in a tax year`
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`body resident` b `under` r MEANS `s 1 "Israeli resident" (b): a body of persons is an Israeli resident in the tax year of` b `under` r

-- (1) incorporated in Israel; (2) control and management of its business exercised in Israel.
#ASSERT `body resident` (`a body in` 2026 `, incorporated in Israel:` TRUE `, control and management in Israel:` `not at all in the tax year`) `under` `D`
#ASSERT `body resident` (`a body in` 2026 `, incorporated in Israel:` FALSE `, control and management in Israel:` `throughout the tax year`) `under` `D`
#ASSERT NOT `body resident` (`a body in` 2026 `, incorporated in Israel:` FALSE `, control and management in Israel:` `not at all in the tax year`) `under` `D`
-- control and management for only part of the tax year: the text is silent (fork PY).
#ASSERT REFUSED `body resident` (`a body in` 2026 `, incorporated in Israel:` FALSE `, control and management in Israel:` `for part of the tax year`) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the body of persons may or may not be an Israeli resident: the text does not say whether control and management in Israel for only part of the tax year, or the ten years of the exception that end inside it, make it one"
#ASSERT `body resident` (`a body in` 2026 `, incorporated in Israel:` FALSE `, control and management in Israel:` `for part of the tax year`) `under` (`the defaults, except part-year connection read` `a connection for any part of the tax year is the connection`)
#ASSERT NOT `body resident` (`a body in` 2026 `, incorporated in Israel:` FALSE `, control and management in Israel:` `for part of the tax year`) `under` (`the defaults, except part-year connection read` `only a connection throughout the tax year is the connection`)
-- incorporated in Israel settles it whatever the part-year fork says
#ASSERT `body resident` (`a body in` 2026 `, incorporated in Israel:` TRUE `, control and management in Israel:` `for part of the tax year`) `under` `D`
#ASSERT REFUSED `body resident` (`a body in` 2023 `, incorporated in Israel:` TRUE `, control and management in Israel:` `throughout the tax year`) `under` `D` BECAUSE "row IL-29 does not hold the text of these provisions for a tax year before 2024"

-- The exception in (b)(2): control and management are exercised in Israel by an individual who became a first-time
-- resident or a veteran returning resident, ten years have not passed since he became a resident, the body would not have
-- been an Israeli resident had the control and management not been so exercised, and the body did not ask otherwise.
GIVEN y     IS A NUMBER
      inc   IS A BOOLEAN
      by    IS A BOOLEAN
      became IS A MAYBE DATE
      elected IS A BOOLEAN
      arrived IS A MAYBE DATE
      cf    IS A BOOLEAN
      asked IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A body of persons in a tax year`
`a body in` y `, incorporated:` inc `, run by such an individual:` by `, who became resident on` became `, elected the adjustment year:` elected `, arrived on` arrived `, not resident but for him:` cf `, asked otherwise:` asked MEANS
    `A body of persons in a tax year` WITH
        `the tax year` IS `the calendar tax year` y
        `it was incorporated in Israel` IS inc
        `the control and management of its business were exercised in Israel` IS `throughout the tax year`
        `the control and management in Israel were exercised by an individual who became a first-time resident or a veteran returning resident, or by someone on his behalf` IS by
        `the day that individual became an Israeli resident` IS became
        `that individual elected the adjustment year of section 14(b)` IS elected
        `the day that individual arrived in Israel` IS arrived
        `it would not have been an Israeli resident had the control and management not been exercised in Israel by such an individual or on his behalf` IS cf
        `the body of persons asked otherwise` IS asked

-- He became a resident on 1 May 2020: ten years run 1 May 2020 - 30 Apr 2030.
--   2026: inside on every reading -> the exception applies -> the body is not a resident.
--   2030 (1 Jan - 31 Dec): whole no; some day yes; last day (31 Dec 2030) no; count: 2030 < 2020 + 10 no -> readings differ -> declined.
--   2031: wholly past the window -> resident (limb (2) is not disapplied).
#ASSERT NOT `body resident` (`a body in` 2026 `, incorporated:` FALSE `, run by such an individual:` TRUE `, who became resident on` (JUST (YMD 2020 5 1)) `, elected the adjustment year:` FALSE `, arrived on` NOTHING `, not resident but for him:` TRUE `, asked otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D`
#ASSERT REFUSED `body resident` (`a body in` 2030 `, incorporated:` FALSE `, run by such an individual:` TRUE `, who became resident on` (JUST (YMD 2020 5 1)) `, elected the adjustment year:` FALSE `, arrived on` NOTHING `, not resident but for him:` TRUE `, asked otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the body of persons may or may not be an Israeli resident: the text does not say whether control and management in Israel for only part of the tax year, or the ten years of the exception that end inside it, make it one"
#ASSERT `body resident` (`a body in` 2031 `, incorporated:` FALSE `, run by such an individual:` TRUE `, who became resident on` (JUST (YMD 2020 5 1)) `, elected the adjustment year:` FALSE `, arrived on` NOTHING `, not resident but for him:` TRUE `, asked otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D`
-- each condition of the proviso, failing in turn: the exception does not apply, so he is resident
#ASSERT `body resident` (`a body in` 2026 `, incorporated:` FALSE `, run by such an individual:` FALSE `, who became resident on` (JUST (YMD 2020 5 1)) `, elected the adjustment year:` FALSE `, arrived on` NOTHING `, not resident but for him:` TRUE `, asked otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D`
#ASSERT `body resident` (`a body in` 2026 `, incorporated:` FALSE `, run by such an individual:` TRUE `, who became resident on` (JUST (YMD 2020 5 1)) `, elected the adjustment year:` FALSE `, arrived on` NOTHING `, not resident but for him:` FALSE `, asked otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D`
#ASSERT `body resident` (`a body in` 2026 `, incorporated:` FALSE `, run by such an individual:` TRUE `, who became resident on` (JUST (YMD 2020 5 1)) `, elected the adjustment year:` FALSE `, arrived on` NOTHING `, not resident but for him:` TRUE `, asked otherwise:` TRUE) `under` `D`
-- incorporated in Israel: limb (1) is not touched by the exception
#ASSERT `body resident` (`a body in` 2026 `, incorporated:` TRUE `, run by such an individual:` TRUE `, who became resident on` (JUST (YMD 2020 5 1)) `, elected the adjustment year:` FALSE `, arrived on` NOTHING `, not resident but for him:` TRUE `, asked otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D`
-- the day he became a resident is needed
#ASSERT REFUSED `body resident` (`a body in` 2026 `, incorporated:` FALSE `, run by such an individual:` TRUE `, who became resident on` NOTHING `, elected the adjustment year:` FALSE `, arrived on` NOTHING `, not resident but for him:` TRUE `, asked otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the exception in paragraph (b)(2) turns on the days that individual arrived in Israel and became an Israeli resident, and they were not given"

-- s 14(b)(2)(b): if he elected the adjustment year, it counts in the ten years, which then run from the day he arrived.
--   Arrived 15 Dec 2019, became a resident 1 May 2020.  Elected: 15 Dec 2019 - 14 Dec 2029.  Not elected: 1 May 2020 - 30 Apr 2030.
--   Tax year 2029: elected -> whole no (31 Dec 2029 > 14 Dec 2029), some yes, last no, count (2029 < 2019 + 10) no -> declined.
--   Not elected -> whole yes, some yes, last yes (31 Dec 2029 <= 30 Apr 2030), count (2029 < 2030) yes -> the exception applies: not resident.
#ASSERT REFUSED `body resident` (`a body in` 2029 `, incorporated:` FALSE `, run by such an individual:` TRUE `, who became resident on` (JUST (YMD 2020 5 1)) `, elected the adjustment year:` TRUE `, arrived on` (JUST (YMD 2019 12 15)) `, not resident but for him:` TRUE `, asked otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the body of persons may or may not be an Israeli resident: the text does not say whether control and management in Israel for only part of the tax year, or the ten years of the exception that end inside it, make it one"
#ASSERT NOT `body resident` (`a body in` 2029 `, incorporated:` FALSE `, run by such an individual:` TRUE `, who became resident on` (JUST (YMD 2020 5 1)) `, elected the adjustment year:` FALSE `, arrived on` (JUST (YMD 2019 12 15)) `, not resident but for him:` TRUE `, asked otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D`
#ASSERT NOT `body resident` (`a body in` 2028 `, incorporated:` FALSE `, run by such an individual:` TRUE `, who became resident on` (JUST (YMD 2020 5 1)) `, elected the adjustment year:` TRUE `, arrived on` (JUST (YMD 2019 12 15)) `, not resident but for him:` TRUE `, asked otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D`
-- elected, but the day he arrived is not given
#ASSERT REFUSED `body resident` (`a body in` 2028 `, incorporated:` FALSE `, run by such an individual:` TRUE `, who became resident on` (JUST (YMD 2020 5 1)) `, elected the adjustment year:` TRUE `, arrived on` NOTHING `, not resident but for him:` TRUE `, asked otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the exception in paragraph (b)(2) turns on the days that individual arrived in Israel and became an Israeli resident, and they were not given"

§ `A foreign resident: not an Israeli resident`

-- A body is a foreign resident exactly when it is not an Israeli resident (the second limb is for individuals).
#ASSERT `s 1 "foreign resident": a body of persons is a foreign resident in the tax year of` (`a body in` 2026 `, incorporated in Israel:` FALSE `, control and management in Israel:` `not at all in the tax year`) `under` `D`
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 "foreign resident": a body of persons is a foreign resident in the tax year of` (`a body in` 2026 `, incorporated in Israel:` TRUE `, control and management in Israel:` `not at all in the tax year`) `under` `D`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      w IS A NUMBER
      p IS A NUMBER
      c IS A MAYBE `Where the centre of life is`
GIVETH A `The absence of an individual in a tax year`
`the absence in` y `: wholly outside` w `days, partly` p `days, centre` c MEANS
    `The absence of an individual in a tax year` WITH
        `the tax year` IS `the calendar tax year` y
        `days wholly outside Israel` IS w
        `days partly in and partly outside Israel` IS p
        `the centre of life, as found` IS c

GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
      ys IS A LIST OF `The absence of an individual in a tax year`
      r  IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`foreign` i `with` ys `under` r MEANS `s 1 "foreign resident": a foreign resident in the tax year of` i `, the tax years' absences being` ys `, under` r

-- He is in Israel by the finding in 2026 (the finding is "in Israel").
`I` MEANS `an individual in` 2026 `, days` 100 `,` 100 `,` 100 `, whose centre of life was found` `in Israel`
-- Not an Israeli resident (finding outside): a foreign resident under the first limb, whatever the absences say (none given).
#ASSERT `foreign` (`an individual in` 2026 `, days` 100 `,` 100 `,` 100 `, whose centre of life was found` `outside Israel`) `with` (LIST) `under` `D`

-- The second limb, pair 2026-2027 (outside Israel 183 days or more in each; the centre of life not in Israel in 2028 and 2029):
--   wholly outside 200 days in 2026 and in 2027 (>= 183); centre of life found outside Israel in 2028 and 2029 -> met.
--   Fork YD: the first year of the pair only -> a foreign resident in 2026; both years -> also (2026 is the first); default: the first
--   year of the pair is met on both readings, so it answers.
`a pair met in 2026 and 2027` MEANS LIST (`the absence in` 2026 `: wholly outside` 200 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `in Israel`)),
                                         (`the absence in` 2027 `: wholly outside` 200 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `in Israel`)),
                                         (`the absence in` 2028 `: wholly outside` 300 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `outside Israel`)),
                                         (`the absence in` 2029 `: wholly outside` 300 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `outside Israel`))
#ASSERT `foreign` `I` `with` `a pair met in 2026 and 2027` `under` `D`
#ASSERT `foreign` `I` `with` `a pair met in 2026 and 2027` `under` (`the defaults, except years deemed read` `the first tax year of the pair only`)
-- He is, at the same time, an Israeli resident by the finding: the definition of "foreign resident" does not unmake that.
#ASSERT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a): an Israeli resident in the tax year of` `I` `under` `D`
-- (a) fails in 2027 (150 days wholly outside): the pair beginning 2026 is not met; he is resident in Israel and not a foreign resident.
`a pair broken in 2027` MEANS LIST (`the absence in` 2026 `: wholly outside` 200 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `in Israel`)),
                                   (`the absence in` 2027 `: wholly outside` 150 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `in Israel`)),
                                   (`the absence in` 2028 `: wholly outside` 300 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `outside Israel`)),
                                   (`the absence in` 2029 `: wholly outside` 300 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `outside Israel`))
#ASSERT NOT `foreign` `I` `with` `a pair broken in 2027` `under` (`the defaults, except years deemed read` `the first tax year of the pair only`)
-- (b) fails: the centre of life was in Israel in 2029
`a centre in Israel in 2029` MEANS LIST (`the absence in` 2026 `: wholly outside` 200 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `in Israel`)),
                                        (`the absence in` 2027 `: wholly outside` 200 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `in Israel`)),
                                        (`the absence in` 2028 `: wholly outside` 300 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `outside Israel`)),
                                        (`the absence in` 2029 `: wholly outside` 300 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `in Israel`))
#ASSERT NOT `foreign` `I` `with` `a centre in Israel in 2029` `under` (`the defaults, except years deemed read` `the first tax year of the pair only`)
-- 183 is enough ("לפחות"); 182 is not
`a pair of 183 and 183 days` MEANS LIST (`the absence in` 2026 `: wholly outside` 183 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `in Israel`)),
                                        (`the absence in` 2027 `: wholly outside` 183 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `in Israel`)),
                                        (`the absence in` 2028 `: wholly outside` 300 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `outside Israel`)),
                                        (`the absence in` 2029 `: wholly outside` 300 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `outside Israel`))
#ASSERT `foreign` `I` `with` `a pair of 183 and 183 days` `under` `D`
`a pair of 183 and 182 days` MEANS LIST (`the absence in` 2026 `: wholly outside` 183 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `in Israel`)),
                                        (`the absence in` 2027 `: wholly outside` 182 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `in Israel`)),
                                        (`the absence in` 2028 `: wholly outside` 300 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `outside Israel`)),
                                        (`the absence in` 2029 `: wholly outside` 300 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `outside Israel`))
#ASSERT NOT `foreign` `I` `with` `a pair of 183 and 182 days` `under` (`the defaults, except years deemed read` `the first tax year of the pair only`)

-- Fork PD: a day partly outside Israel.  180 days wholly outside and 5 partly in 2026; 200 wholly in 2027.
--   Wholly only: 180 < 183 -> not met.  With the partly-out days: 185 >= 183 -> met.  The default declines.
`a pair with five partial days in 2026` MEANS LIST (`the absence in` 2026 `: wholly outside` 180 `days, partly` 5 `days, centre` (JUST `in Israel`)),
                                                   (`the absence in` 2027 `: wholly outside` 200 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `in Israel`)),
                                                   (`the absence in` 2028 `: wholly outside` 300 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `outside Israel`)),
                                                   (`the absence in` 2029 `: wholly outside` 300 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `outside Israel`))
#ASSERT REFUSED `foreign` `I` `with` `a pair with five partial days in 2026` `under` (`the defaults, except years deemed read` `the first tax year of the pair only`) BECAUSE "the second limb of the definition of foreign resident may or may not be met: the text does not say for which tax year it deems the individual a foreign resident (the first of the pair or both), or whether a day partly outside Israel is a day outside Israel"
#ASSERT `foreign` `I` `with` `a pair with five partial days in 2026` `under` (`the defaults, except partial day read` `a day partly outside Israel is a day outside Israel` `and years deemed read` `the first tax year of the pair only`)
#ASSERT NOT `foreign` `I` `with` `a pair with five partial days in 2026` `under` (`the defaults, except partial day read` `a day partly outside Israel is not a day outside Israel` `and years deemed read` `the first tax year of the pair only`)

-- Fork YD, the other pair.  Pair 2025-2026 is met (200 and 200 days outside; the centre of life outside Israel in 2027 and
-- 2028); pair 2026-2027 is not (only 100 days wholly outside in 2027).  Is he a foreign resident in 2026?
--   the first year of the pair only: the pair that begins in 2026 is not met -> not a foreign resident;
--   both years of the pair: the pair that begins in 2025 includes 2026 -> a foreign resident;   default: declined.
`the pair 2025-2026 met, the pair 2026-2027 not` MEANS LIST (`the absence in` 2025 `: wholly outside` 200 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `in Israel`)),
                                                           (`the absence in` 2026 `: wholly outside` 200 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `in Israel`)),
                                                           (`the absence in` 2027 `: wholly outside` 100 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `outside Israel`)),
                                                           (`the absence in` 2028 `: wholly outside` 300 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `outside Israel`)),
                                                           (`the absence in` 2029 `: wholly outside` 300 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `outside Israel`))
#ASSERT NOT `foreign` `I` `with` `the pair 2025-2026 met, the pair 2026-2027 not` `under` (`the defaults, except years deemed read` `the first tax year of the pair only`)
#ASSERT `foreign` `I` `with` `the pair 2025-2026 met, the pair 2026-2027 not` `under` (`the defaults, except years deemed read` `both tax years of the pair`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `foreign` `I` `with` `the pair 2025-2026 met, the pair 2026-2027 not` `under` `D` BECAUSE "the second limb of the definition of foreign resident may or may not be met: the text does not say for which tax year it deems the individual a foreign resident (the first of the pair or both), or whether a day partly outside Israel is a day outside Israel"
-- Facts not given for a tax year the limb needs.
#ASSERT REFUSED `foreign` `I` `with` (LIST) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the second limb of the definition of foreign resident turns on the days outside Israel and the finding of the centre of life in neighbouring tax years, and the facts of one of them were not given"
-- (b) asks where the centre of life was by paragraph (a)(1): a finding.  None for 2028, though (a) is met:
`a pair whose centre of life in 2028 is not found` MEANS LIST (`the absence in` 2026 `: wholly outside` 200 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `in Israel`)),
                                                              (`the absence in` 2027 `: wholly outside` 200 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `in Israel`)),
                                                              (`the absence in` 2028 `: wholly outside` 300 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` NOTHING),
                                                              (`the absence in` 2029 `: wholly outside` 300 `days, partly` 0 `days, centre` (JUST `outside Israel`))
#ASSERT REFUSED `foreign` `I` `with` `a pair whose centre of life in 2028 is not found` `under` (`the defaults, except years deemed read` `the first tax year of the pair only`) BECAUSE "paragraph (b) of the second limb asks where the centre of life was, as stated in paragraph (a)(1) of the definition of Israeli resident, and no finding for that tax year was given"
